VERDICT: PASS -- the limb run 1 could not reach is measured. A named hardware management ACL bound with `access-group` to both management ingress ports survives a 60 s cold boot with both halves enforced: the non-specified host's SYNs to management SSH are still dropped silently in hardware (4 sent, 0 replies, ICMP 4 of 4 to the same address) and the user-specified host still completes its handshake (4 `SA`), before anything is typed into the device. Taken with run 1, T33386 is PASS with its reboot-persistence limb MEASURED.
